  "answer": "This feature request (a scheduled Awake mode with start/end times and days of the week) has been reported before and is being tracked centrally in PowerToys#24846. Several duplicates, including #27790, #45602 and #30310, were closed in favor of it. It is not available yet, so please thumbs-up #24846 to help prioritize it. As a workaround, you can launch Awake from the CLI with an expiry time, e.g. `PowerToys.Awake.exe --expire-at=17:30:00 --display-on=false`. One user automated this with a Windows scheduled task that triggers a PowerShell script on resume from sleep. The script kills any running Awake process and restarts it with the expiry set to the end of the workday."
